WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.917
Six forty-seven p.m. Mr. Pawar walks into the community centre, shaking.

2
00:00:06.417 --> 00:00:13.521
A man from the courier company called. I paid thirty-eight thousand rupees, and now his phone is off.

3
00:00:14.121 --> 00:00:21.041
Farah is the First Responder here. She does not investigate. She asks six questions.

4
00:00:21.441 --> 00:00:31.638
What happened? When? Was money involved? Is anyone in danger? Is it still happening? What evidence is there?

5
00:00:32.138 --> 00:00:35.393
At six twelve. Thirty-five minutes ago.

6
00:00:35.993 --> 00:00:43.110
Money lost within the hour, and nobody in danger. So this is an amber case. Urgent.

7
00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:51.736
Stop all payments. Save the transaction ID and the caller's number. Then call nineteen thirty, now.

8
00:00:53.736 --> 00:00:59.387
The complaint is in. The bank can now try to hold the money, while it is still moving.

9
00:01:00.587 --> 00:01:08.235
Every case gets a colour. Red: someone's safety is at risk. Call one one two, at once.

10
00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:13.766
Amber: money lost in the last day. Call nineteen thirty within the hour.

11
00:01:14.366 --> 00:01:20.856
Yellow: an older loss, a fake profile, or harassment. Report on the portal the same day.

12
00:01:21.456 --> 00:01:28.289
Green: a suspicious message, and nothing lost. Report it on Chakshu, and give advice.

13
00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:37.638
Identify. Stabilise. Preserve. Route. And never promise that the money will come back.
